### D8 — Relay `backend/server.js`
```js
const SERVER_RELAY_TOKEN = process.env.RELAY_TOKEN;
if (!SERVER_RELAY_TOKEN) { console.error('RELAY_TOKEN env var is required'); process.exit(1); }

// challenge bound to the socket, not to a deviceId
case 'GET_CHALLENGE': { ws.challenge = { value: crypto.randomBytes(32).toString('hex'), ts: Date.now() };
  return safeSend(ws, { type: 'AUTH_CHALLENGE', payload: { challenge: ws.challenge.value } }); }

// in REGISTER_DEVICE after the signature verifies:
const prev = knownKeys.get(deviceId);                  // const knownKeys = new Map(); persist to disk/DB in production
if (prev && prev !== publicKey) return safeSend(ws, { type: 'ERROR', message: 'Key mismatch for deviceId' });
knownKeys.set(deviceId, publicKey);
ws.authDeviceId = deviceId;

// in every forwarding case:
if (!ws.authDeviceId) return safeSend(ws, { type: 'ERROR', message: 'Not registered' });
// ... fromDeviceId: ws.authDeviceId     (NEVER payload.senderDeviceId)
```
Also: serve only behind TLS (Nginx/Caddy `wss://`), remove counts from `/health`, keep rate-limit and 32 KB limit. Document `RELAY_TOKEN=<long random> node server.js`. Update the Android `RelayClient` accordingly (it must send the same token via `store.relayToken`).

### D9 — Update downloader (recommended, M3)
Manifest: `REQUEST_INSTALL_PACKAGES` + `FileProvider`. Download the APK with OkHttp to `cacheDir`, verify SHA-256 against `checksumSha256` (skip only if blank), verify `packageArchiveInfo.packageName == packageName` and signing certificate equals the installed app's, then install through `FileProvider` + `ACTION_VIEW`. Allow only `https` URLs. Keep the current browser fallback when the file cannot be verified. Works for both Storage URLs and direct links.

