```

**Rule-design notes for the agent:** `licenseOk()` uses `existsAfter/getAfter` so the activation transaction (license + user + device written together) is validated as one unit. A normal user can set premium fields only when a license exists that (a) belongs to them, (b) is not revoked, (c) lists **this** device in `boundDevices`, and (d) matches the tier. `expiresAt` on a device may only mirror the license's `expiresAt`. A license update by a normal user may touch only `userId,isUsed,boundDevices,expiresAt,lastUsedAt`, may add at most one device, never exceeds `maxDevices`, and the first activation may not set an expiry beyond `now + durationDays`.
Write rule unit tests with `@firebase/rules-unit-testing` + the emulator for at least the cases in PART I §I.2.

