## PART K — Known limits (be honest with the owner)

- Firebase Storage upload may not work on the Spark plan for new projects; the direct-link method is the guaranteed path.
- Notifications cannot reach the app without a receiver (FCM needs a trusted sender; Cloud Functions need Blaze). In-app polling of a Firestore collection is the Spark-compatible option (D10).
- Anonymous accounts are tied to the install; reinstall needs "Reset Binding" until Google/Email linking is added.
- Real-time behaviour depends on Firestore snapshot listeners already present in `LicenseManager`; offline devices apply changes on reconnect.
- APK signing key loss = no more updates for existing installs. Back it up.
